.TH TBL 1
.SH NAME
tbl \- typeset tables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tbl
[
.B -ms
] [
.B -mm
] [
.B -TX
] [
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tbl
is a preprocessor for
.IR troff (1):
each table in its
.I files
(or its standard input), between
.B .TS
and
.BR .TE ,
is turned into what troff sets it by; the rest is passed on.
A table is its options (ending in
.BR ; :
.BR center ,
.BR box ,
.BR allbox ,
.BR tab( x )
and others), the formats of its columns (ending in
.BR . :
.B l
.B r
.B c
.B n
.B s
.B ^
.BR _ ,
fonts and widths), then its rows, the cells apart by tabs:
.IP
.EX
\&.TS
center box;
c s
l n.
Philosophers
_
Plato	347
Aristotle	322
\&.TE
.EE
.PP
It is a translation of Plan 9's
.IR tbl ;
for the same input its output is, byte for byte, Plan 9's.
Under
.B -mbook
a table's rules are drawn as lines
.RB ( .rules
in
.IR troff (1)).
.TP
.B -ms
.TP
.B -mm
Read the macros first.
.TP
.B -TX
For a printer without fractional motions.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/tbl
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR troff (1)
.br
M. E. Lesk, \(lqTbl \(em A Program to Format Tables\(rq.
